      "raw_description": "INDmoney is hiring Product Interns for a 6-month internship. Pre-placement offer (PPO) based on performance during internship. Please note: This is a mandatory 6-month, full-time, on-site internship in Gurugram. You will be receiving an internship compensation on a monthly basis. Apply only if you can commit to the full 6 months on-site. About INDmoney INDmoney enables Indians to invest and trade across the world (including India) and manage their Networth. INDmoney is a pioneer and leader for Indians to access US markets from India. The role: For 6 months, you’ll work as Product Associate - not as a shadow. You’ll own real product work alongside senior Product Managers. What you’ll do: Own a feature or product area from idea to launch. Define problems clearly and write PRDs with user stories, edge cases and success metrics. Work daily with engineering and design to plan sprints, unblock the team and ship on time. Track how your features perform using SQL and analytics tools, and use the data to decide next steps. Help design and analyse A/B tests. Coordinate launches with marketing, compliance and customer support. Share regular updates on progress, results and learnings with your team and leadership. What we’re looking for: Final-year students or recent graduates (B.Tech (Computer Science), MBA (Top tier) or similar) Should have had learning on building consumer facing Tech products/ apps/ Web interfaces/ or core Tech systems. Very comfortable data, analytics and databases. Clear, structured thinking and writing; you can explain a problem and your solution simply. Ownership and drive; you follow through without being chased. Extremely familiar with with tools like Figma, Mixpanel or Jira etc. Available for the full 6 months, full-time and on-site in Gurugram (mandatory). What you’ll get: Real ownership of work that ships to millions of users. Direct mentorship from experienced Product Managers. Deep exposure to fintech, consumer behaviour, how to to build in regulated environments. Possibility of PPO - based on performance during the internship.",
