      "description": "Junior Data Analyst Location: India (Remote) Experience: 0-1 year | Fresh graduates are welcome About Leadership Retros Leadership Retros brings together senior business and technology leaders through curated CXO conversations, executive communities and invite-only leadership exp...",
      "raw_description": "Junior Data Analyst Location: India (Remote) Experience: 0-1 year | Fresh graduates are welcome About Leadership Retros Leadership Retros brings together senior business and technology leaders through curated CXO conversations, executive communities and invite-only leadership experiences. Behind these experiences is a growing amount of data — from executive profiles and outreach activity to registrations, engagement and event performance. We’re looking for a Junior Data Analyst who can help us turn that data into clear, useful insights. If you enjoy working with numbers, spotting patterns and making sense of information, this could be a strong starting point for your career in analytics. What You’ll Do Collect, clean and organise data from multiple internal sources. Maintain structured datasets related to executives, companies, outreach, registrations and events. Analyse data to identify trends, patterns and useful business insights. Create regular reports and dashboards for internal teams. Track metrics such as outreach performance, response rates, registrations, attendance and engagement. Identify missing, duplicate or inconsistent data and help improve data quality. Support segmentation of prospects based on company, industry, seniority, location and other relevant parameters. Work with teams across research, outreach and events to understand their reporting needs. Prepare clear summaries and visualisations that make data easy to understand. Support ad-hoc analysis for upcoming events, campaigns and executive engagement initiatives. Who We’re Looking For 0-1 year of experience in data analysis, reporting or a related area. Fresh graduates with strong analytical skills are encouraged to apply. Good knowledge of Microsoft Excel or Google Sheets . Comfortable working with formulas, filters, lookups, pivot tables and data cleaning. Strong attention to detail and accuracy. Ability to interpret data and communicate findings clearly. Logical, structured and curious approach to problem-solving. Comfortable working independently in a remote environment. Good to Have Basic knowledge of SQL . Exposure to Power BI, Tableau, Looker Studio or similar visualisation tools . Basic understanding of Python for data analysis. Experience through internships, academic projects or personal analytics projects. Familiarity with CRM, marketing or event-related datasets. What You’ll Gain This role gives you exposure to real business data rather than only theoretical analysis. You’ll get the opportunity to work with data connected to executive engagement, events, outreach and business decision-making , while developing practical skills across: Data cleaning and validation Reporting and dashboards Business analytics Data visualisation Performance tracking Insight generation Why Join At Leadership Retros, you’ll work in a fast-moving environment where your analysis can directly influence how we identify audiences, improve outreach and build better leadership experiences. You don’t need years of experience. If you’re analytical, detail-oriented and excited to turn data into meaningful insights, we’d love to hear from you.",
