      "description": "At Bristol Myers Squibb, our employees often ask, “Who are you working for?”—a question that fuels collaboration, accountability, and urgency in our work. Our purpose-driven culture inspires us to discover, develop, and deliver innovative medicines to prevail over serious disease...",
      "raw_description": "At Bristol Myers Squibb, our employees often ask, “Who are you working for?”—a question that fuels collaboration, accountability, and urgency in our work. Our purpose-driven culture inspires us to discover, develop, and deliver innovative medicines to prevail over serious diseases. We offer uniquely interesting and meaningful work, opportunities for growth, and a supportive environment that values inclusion, wellbeing, flexibility, and comprehensive benefits. This is work that transforms the lives of patients, and the careers of those who do it. Analytics Delivery & AI Enablement Support the development and delivery of analytical solutions under the guidance of senior analysts and team leads. Apply foundational analytics, decision science, and AI/ML techniques to support Ex-US Commercial initiatives across brand strategy, omnichannel engagement, and resource allocation. Translate well-defined business questions into analytical tasks, execute analyses, and summarize findings. Ensure accuracy, quality, and adherence to analytical best practices in all deliverables. Stakeholder Support & Business Understanding Collaborate with Ex-US Commercial stakeholders, Global Analytics, OCx, Marketing, and BIT to understand business context and analytical requirements. Support preparation of analytical outputs, presentations, and dashboards for stakeholder discussions. Clearly communicate results, assumptions, and limitations with guidance from senior team members. Incorporate stakeholder feedback to refine analyses and outputs. Omnichannel & Commercial Analytics Execute analytics supporting personal and non-personal promotion channels, including field force, email, web, paid media, social, and third-party platforms. Support development and tracking of performance metrics related to reach, engagement, and effectiveness. Assist in test-and-learn initiatives, A/B tests, and basic quasi-experimental analyses. Identify trends, anomalies, and opportunities in data and escalate insights to senior team members. Team Collaboration & Learning Work collaboratively within project teams, contributing to shared goals and timelines. Learn and adopt standard analytical frameworks, tools, and coding best practices used by the team. Participate in knowledge-sharing sessions and training programs. Demonstrate curiosity and initiative in developing analytical and business skills. Technical Execution & Data Handling Build and maintain datasets, basic models, dashboards, and recurring reports. Perform data validation, quality checks, and documentation of analytical processes. Work with data engineering and BIT teams to understand data structures and resolve data issues. Follow established governance, compliance, and documentation standards. Skills & Competencies Strong analytical mindset with attention to detail and data quality. Good written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to explain analyses in simple terms. Ability to manage assigned tasks effectively and meet deadlines. Willingness to learn new tools, techniques, and business concepts. Collaborative and proactive team player with a positive attitude. Basic problem-solving skills and ability to apply structured thinking. Experience & Qualifications BA/BS required; degrees in life sciences, computer science, mathematics, statistics, data science, or engineering preferred. 1–3 years of professional experience in analytics, data analysis, decision science, or related roles. Experience working with structured datasets and performing quantitative analyses. Exposure to commercial analytics, marketing analytics, or healthcare/pharmaceutical analytics is a plus. Interest in applying data, analytics, and AI to solve real-world business problems. Technical Skills (Preferred) Hands-on experience with Python and/or R for data analysis and basic modelling. Familiarity with statistical concepts and introductory machine learning techniques. Experience with data visualization and reporting tools (e.g., R Shiny, Dash, Tableau, Power BI, or similar). Exposure to collaborative analytics environments (e.g., Databricks, Git, SharePoint). Basic understanding of omnichannel, digital marketing, or commercial data sources. We hire for skills and capabilities, not just credentials – if this role excites you, but doesn’t perfectly match your resume, we encourage you to apply anyway. How We Work Where you work matters – because collaboration, innovation and patient impact happen in many settings. Our roles are structured across four work models: site-essential, site-by-design, field-based and remote-by-design. The model assigned to this role is based on its core responsibilities. Learn more at https://careers.bms.com/ways-of-working. Supporting People With Disabilities BMS is dedicated to ensuring that people with disabilities can excel through a transparent recruitment process, reasonable workplace accommodations/adjustments and ongoing support in their roles. Applicants can request a reasonable workplace accommodation/adjustment prior to accepting a job offer. If you require reasonable accommodations/adjustments in completing this application, or in any part of the recruitment process, direct your inquiries to adastaffingsupport@bms.com. Visit careers.bms.com/eeo-accessibility to access our complete Equal Employment Opportunity statement. Candidate Rights BMS will consider qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, pursuant to applicable laws in your area. For roles based in Los Angeles County only: If you live in or expect to work from Los Angeles County if hired for this position, please visit this page for important additional information: https://careers.bms.com/california-residents/ For roles based in Washington State only: If you live in or expect to work from Washington State if hired for this position, please visit this page for important information about the Washington Fair Chance Act. Data Protection We will never request payments, financial information, or social security numbers during our application or recruitment process. Learn more about protecting yourself at https://careers.bms.com/fraud-protection. Any data processed in connection with role applications will be treated in accordance with applicable data privacy policies and regulations. If this posting is missing required information required by local law or incorrect, contact BMS at TAEnablement@bms.com with the Job Title and Requisition number. Do not send application-related inquiries to this email. To check your application status, please login to your Candidate Home Account. R1602754 : Analyst, Non-US Advanced Analytics & Decision Intelligence",
