      "description": "Job Description Job Roles and Responsibilities : Conduct regular visits to assigned schools as per the planned schedule to provide on-ground support to teachers and headmasters. Guide and handhold teachers and headmasters in effectively using the NIPUN Maharashtra App for conduct...",
      "raw_description": "Job Description Job Roles and Responsibilities : Conduct regular visits to assigned schools as per the planned schedule to provide on-ground support to teachers and headmasters. Guide and handhold teachers and headmasters in effectively using the NIPUN Maharashtra App for conducting Foundational Literacy and Numeracy (FLN) assessments. Identify and resolve on-ground challenges related to app usage, data entry, connectivity, device functionality, and other technical issues. Record videos of students and teachers using the application for training, monitoring, and documentation purposes, strictly adhering to VOPA’s and the school's child safeguarding and consent protocols. Establish and maintain effective working relationships with teachers, headmasters, and other school-level stakeholders to ensure smooth implementation of the project. Monitor application usage, assessment activities, and school-wise progress across assigned schools. Identify and report school-level challenges, implementation gaps, and feedback to the core NIPUN Project Team for timely resolution. Maintain accurate school visit records, visit logs, and school-wise documentation. Assist in preparing visit summaries, progress reports, and other required reports. Support SCERT and district-level correspondence and coordination related to assigned schools, as and when required. Provide timely updates and regular reports to the Program Team regarding school-wise implementation status, progress, and challenges. Identify and escalate field-level challenges at an early stage, including internet connectivity issues, device-related problems, teacher hesitation, and other implementation constraints. Conduct testing of VOPA applications to identify bugs, usability issues, and functional gaps, and report findings to the concerned technical team. Undertake any other duties, responsibilities, assignments, or research-related tasks as may reasonably be assigned by the Reporting Manager from time to time. Salary Range 20,000 - 24,000 p.m.",
