      "description": "About Triomics: Triomics helps oncology organizations scale clinical research and high-quality data creation without scaling headcount. Our AI platform - powered by OncoLLM™- automates the operational work behind trial screening, eligibility interpretation, and oncology data abst...",
      "raw_description": "About Triomics: Triomics helps oncology organizations scale clinical research and high-quality data creation without scaling headcount. Our AI platform - powered by OncoLLM™- automates the operational work behind trial screening, eligibility interpretation, and oncology data abstraction across Prism (clinical trial matching), Harmony (oncology registry + RWE curation), and Symphony (clinician copilot). Built for real-world hospital workflows, Triomics integrates with EHRs and CTMS systems and is deployed with leading academic cancer centers to improve speed, consistency, and audit-ready clinical accuracy. Responsibilities: Coordinate with multiple developers, designers and business team to take requirements, drive schedules, communicate technical requirements, and review and test end-to-end functionality Writing product requirement documents after conducting user research using multiple channels including but not limited to surveys, calling, interviews, FGDs and analyzing the data present in the system Analyze the data present in the system and derive insights to make business critical decisions Create design briefs and collaborate with the design team to create wireframes and designs Review and report on key performance indicators as decided mutually with the reporting manager Manage the day-to-day operations in the product life-cycle, simultaneously own the vision of the organization Required Qualifications: More than one year of work experience working as an Associate Product Manager Good communication skills, organizational and problem solving skills with great attention to detail, including the ability to track multiple development executions simultaneously and analyze the results An understanding and empathy for users The ability to structure and analyze ambiguous problems and the ability to communicate ideas clearly through workflows, feature descriptions etc. The candidate must be self-motivated and driven with a go-getter attitude. He/she must be persuasive without being forceful Working knowledge of SQL and presentation tools like Power BI, Microstrategy, etc. is good to have Perks & Benefits: Lunch Provided at the Office – one less daily decision, one happier employee. Flexible Working Hours – we care about output, not clock-ins. Health Insurance – comprehensive coverage for you and your family. Zomato Meal Benefit – breakfast and dinner can be ordered when you come in early or leave late, because effort deserves fuel.",
