      "description": "Our Company: At Teradata, we believe that people thrive when empowered with better information.  Teradata Autonomous Knowledge Platform activates enterprise intelligence by unifying data, knowledge and business context to achieve tangible outcomes.  With Teradata, organizations c...",
      "raw_description": "Our Company: At Teradata, we believe that people thrive when empowered with better information.  Teradata Autonomous Knowledge Platform activates enterprise intelligence by unifying data, knowledge and business context to achieve tangible outcomes.  With Teradata, organizations can provide agents with full context for impact when it matters.  Our solution lets businesses connect and scale on premises, in the cloud, or through a hybrid approach.  Teradata delivers real business value with AI. About The Role Teradata's Digital Operations team manages web content production, campaign operations, and digital marketing systems across global markets.  We're looking for a project coordinator/manager intern who is curious about artificial intelligence, energized by process improvement, and eager to do real work — not shadow work. In this role, you won't just observe.  You'll map how our team actually works, identify where AI-assisted tools can reduce friction, build a proof-of-concept workflow, and present your findings to the broader team.  You'll leave with a concrete portfolio artifact and a working understanding of how enterprise digital operations function at scale. What You'll Do Coordinate and track active projects across content, creative, and digital development workstreams, using our existing project management tools Shadow content and campaign production workflows to document current-state processes (intake, review, approval, localization, publishing) Identify repetitive, manual, or high-friction tasks that are candidates for AI-assisted improvement Research and evaluate AI tools relevant to content operations, copywriting, translation, or project tracking Design and prototype an improved workflow — including a prompt library, template system, or process playbook — as your capstone deliverable Present your findings, recommendations, and prototype to Digital Operations leadership at the end of your internship Contribute to live projects as bandwidth allows — briefing, copy QA, asset tracking, or localization coordination Capstone project: AI-assisted content operations audit and playbook Overview Your primary deliverable is an AI process improvement playbook built from original research inside the Digital Operations team.  This is not a theoretical exercise — you will document real workflows, test real tools, and propose changes the team can actually implement. Phase 1 — Discovery (weeks 1–3) Interview team members across content, creative, and digital development to map current-state workflows Document 3–5 high-volume, recurring production tasks (e. g. , web manuscript drafting, stakeholder routing, localization kickoffs, asset QA) Identify pain points: where do tasks stall, where is effort duplicated, where does quality vary? Produce a current-state process map for at least two workflows Phase 2 — Analysis and tool evaluation (weeks 4–7) Research AI tools relevant to the identified friction points — consider categories including generative writing, translation/localization, project routing, structured data extraction, and QA automation Evaluate 3–5 tools against team needs, security considerations, and integration feasibility Define success criteria: what does a better workflow look like, and how would we measure improvement? Present a mid-point summary and recommendation to your manager Phase 3 — Prototype and build (weeks 8–10) Design a future-state workflow for your highest-priority process Build a proof of concept — this could be a prompt library, a structured intake template, an AI-assisted content brief system, a RACI-integrated routing guide, or another artifact suited to your findings Test the prototype with at least one team member and document feedback Phase 4 — Documentation and presentation (weeks 11–12) Produce a written playbook: current state, recommended changes, prototype overview, adoption guide, and measurement framework Deliver a final presentation to Digital Operations leadership — 20 minutes plus Q&A Hand off all artifacts in formats the team can immediately use Who You Are Enrolled in an undergraduate or graduate program in business, communications, marketing, information systems, operations, or a related field Comfortable asking questions and talking to people — a big part of this role is listening and documenting what you hear Genuinely curious about AI tools and how they apply to real work (hands-on experience is a plus, but curiosity matters more) Experience using AI writing or productivity tools (Claude, Copilot, Trello, etc. ) Organized and detail-oriented — you track your own work and flag issues before they become problems Strong written communicator — you can turn a messy conversation into a clean summary Familiar with at least one project management or collaboration tool (Jira, Trello, Confluence, Sharepoint, or similar) Preferred (but Not Required) Familiarity with content production, editorial, or marketing workflows Exposure to localization or multi-language content operations Experience creating process documentation, SOPs, or workflow diagrams What You'll Gain A portfolio-ready capstone project you fully own — from research to presentation Hands-on exposure to enterprise digital marketing and content operations Practical experience evaluating and applying AI tools in a professional context Mentorship from practitioners in digital operations, content strategy, and campaign management A clear view into what project coordination and operations management look like in a global B2B technology company Why We Think You’ll Love Teradata We prioritize a people-first culture because we know our people are at the very heart of our success. We embrace a flexible work model because we trust our people to make decisions about how, when, and where they work. We focus on well-being because we care about our people and their ability to thrive both personally and professionally. We are an anti-racist company because our dedication to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion is more than a statement. It is a deep commitment to doing the work to foster an equitable environment that celebrates people for all of who they are. Teradata invites all identities and backgrounds in the workplace. We work with deliberation and intent to ensure we are cultivating collaboration and inclusivity across our global organization. ​ We are proud to be an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer. We do not discriminate based upon race, color, ancestry, religion, creed, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, breastfeeding, or related conditions), national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, medical condition, genetic information, gender identity or expression, military and veteran status, or any other legally protected status.",
