      "description": "Date Posted: 2026-11-16 Country: India Location: IN-TS-HYDERABAD-B3F7 ~ DLF Cybercity Gachibowli ~ DLF CYBERCITY GACHIBOWLI-B3F7, 7th Fl in Block 3 Position Role Type: Hybrid Job Description At RTX, the world's largest aerospace and defense company, 185,000 great minds are united...",
      "raw_description": "Date Posted: 2026-11-16 Country: India Location: IN-TS-HYDERABAD-B3F7 ~ DLF Cybercity Gachibowli ~ DLF CYBERCITY GACHIBOWLI-B3F7, 7th Fl in Block 3 Position Role Type: Hybrid Job Description At RTX, the world's largest aerospace and defense company, 185,000 great minds are united by purpose and inspired to make a difference solving the world’s most complex problems. With our three market leading businesses, world-class operations and investments in research and development, we offer capabilities and opportunity no one else can. Together, we push the boundaries of known science and find new ways to connect and protect our world. Collins Aerospace is a leader in technologically advanced, intelligent solutions that help redefine the aerospace and defense industry. With a comprehensive portfolio and deep technical expertise, we help customers meet the demands of the global market. Join us and help shape the future of aerospace and defense. Overview We are looking for an enthusiastic and curious Associate Engineer – Applied AI to join our AI Enablement & Automation (AEA) team at Collins Aerospace. This is an entry-level engineering opportunity for someone passionate about software development, Artificial Intelligence, and emerging technologies. You will contribute to building AI-powered applications that address real-world engineering and business challenges. You will work alongside experienced engineers, technical leads, and architects to explore AI capabilities, develop application components, build prototypes, and learn how AI solutions are developed and deployed in enterprise environments. We value strong programming fundamentals, analytical thinking, curiosity, and the ability to learn quickly over extensive experience with specific AI frameworks. This role offers an opportunity to develop specialized skills in Generative AI, Agentic AI, and Applied AI engineering. Key Responsibilities Software & AI Application Development Develop application components using Python and modern software development practices. Assist in building AI-powered applications using Large Language Models (LLMs) and other AI technologies. Work with structured and unstructured data to support AI application development. Write clean, maintainable, and reusable code. AI Experimentation & Prototyping Explore emerging AI technologies and experiment with different models and approaches. Build prototypes and proof-of-concepts to validate ideas and demonstrate AI capabilities. Experiment with prompt engineering and basic LLM workflows. Support the development of chatbots, copilots, and RAG-based applications. Integration & Engineering Practices Assist in developing backend services and integrating REST APIs. Work with databases and data processing components. Use Git and established software development workflows. Participate in testing, debugging, and code reviews. Learning & Collaboration Work closely with senior engineers, architects, and technical leads. Participate in sprint planning, technical discussions, and engineering demonstrations. Learn and adopt new AI technologies, frameworks, and development practices. Take ownership of assigned tasks and deliver them with guidance from experienced team members. Qualifications You Must Have Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Artificial Intelligence, or a related engineering discipline. Programming Fundamentals Good programming fundamentals in Python. Working knowledge of at least one additional programming language, such as Java, C++, or JavaScript. Understanding of Object-Oriented Programming (OOP), data structures, and basic algorithms. Familiarity with basic software development and debugging practices. AI & Machine Learning Fundamentals Basic understanding of Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, and Generative AI concepts. Awareness of Large Language Models (LLMs) and their applications. Basic understanding of prompt engineering and how AI models can be used to solve practical problems. Software Development Fundamentals Basic understanding of REST APIs and application development. Familiarity with databases and handling structured or unstructured data. Exposure to Git or other version control systems. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. Curiosity and willingness to explore emerging technologies. Ability to learn new programming languages, tools, and frameworks quickly. Good communication and collaboration skills. A proactive approach to learning, experimentation, and continuous improvement. Qualifications We Prefer The following qualifications are desirable but not mandatory: Academic projects, internships, or personal projects involving AI, Machine Learning, or Python development. Exposure to LLM APIs such as OpenAI, Azure AI, Gemini, Claude, or similar platforms. Familiarity with AI development frameworks such as LangChain or LangGraph. Basic exposure to PyTorch, TensorFlow, or Scikit-learn. Experience building simple chatbots, AI assistants, or RAG-based prototypes. Familiarity with Docker, cloud platforms, or CI/CD concepts. Exposure to Computer Vision or Natural Language Processing. What We Offer Opportunity to work on real-world AI applications with measurable engineering and business impact. Hands-on exposure to Generative AI, Agentic AI, and emerging technologies. Mentorship from experienced engineers, architects, and technical leads. Opportunities to develop skills across the AI application development lifecycle. Continuous learning and professional development. Collaborative and technically driven engineering culture. Flexible hybrid work model. WE ARE REDEFINING AEROSPACE. Some of our competitive benefits packages include: Transportation facility. Meal coupons o Group Term Life Insurance. Group Health Insurance. Group Personal Accident Insurance. Entitled for 18 days of vacation and 12 days of sick leave annually. Employee scholar program Work life balance o Car lease program National Pension Scheme LTA o Fuel & Maintenance /Driver wages Meal vouchers And more! Nothing matters more to Collins Aerospace than our strong ethical and safety commitments. As such, all India positions require a background check, which may include a drug screen. At Collins, the paths we pave together lead to limitless possibilities. And the bonds we form – with our customers and with each other -- propel us all higher, again and again. RTX adheres to the principles of equal employment. All qualified applications will be given careful consideration without regard to ethnicity, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation or identity, national origin, age, disability, protected veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law. Privacy Policy and Terms: Click on this link to read the Policy and Terms",
