      "raw_description": "About Testlify Testlify helps companies hire on skills. Recruiters use our tests to see what candidates can do before the interview. We also run the company with AI. AI agents already do real work across sales, operations and marketing here. Many of them started as a quick first version. Your job is to make them solid. The harness we are building Most teams use AI tools as they come. We are building a harness around them: a layer that makes the AI faster and keeps its output to the standard we need. Today it does these things: Rules on every step. The AI follows set rules, and automatic checks run before and after each action. If a step skips a rule, the check blocks it and the AI redoes it. Plan before action. Before the AI changes a file or sends anything, it writes down what it will do and how it will check the result. Memory. The AI remembers past decisions, corrections and how we like things done, so we do not repeat ourselves. Skills. Reusable playbooks for common jobs, so the AI does a task the same way every time. Structured builds. New features go from a written spec to a build round, a fix round, tests and a release gate. A desktop app. Chat with the AI, a terminal, code changes and a file editor in one window. The job A first version that works on a good day is easy to build with AI. One that works every day, on messy data, without someone watching it, is hard. That is your job. You will write real code. You will connect agents to the tools the team already uses, make them fail safely, and make them cheap and fast enough to run every day. What you will do Build agents and tools in Python or TypeScript on top of large language model APIs. Connect agents to the systems the team works in, such as email, documents, spreadsheets and project trackers, through APIs and tool connectors. Add the parts a demo skips: retries, logging, alerts, tests and a clear way to undo a mistake. Make agents faster and cheaper. Measure cost and time per run, then cut both. Add new checks and features to the harness itself, with tests, through build and fix rounds. Review code that AI wrote. Catch what it got wrong before it ships. What you will work on Kind of work- What a task looks like Data pipelines - Pull data from many public sources that each break in their own way. Keep every source working and flag the ones that stop. Integrations- Let an agent read and write in the tools the team uses, with the right access and nothing more. Reliability- Take an agent that fails one run in ten and find out why. Fix it so it fails safely, or not at all. Scheduled agents - Move a job someone runs by hand onto a schedule, with alerts when it goes wrong. Harness features- Build a new rule or check into the harness, test it, and ship it through the release gate. Cost and speed- Find the slow or costly step in a workflow and make it cheaper without losing quality. You might be a fit if You are a final-year student or recent graduate of an IIT, in computer science or any branch where you wrote a lot of code. You have shipped code that other people used: a project, an open-source fix, an internship, a hackathon build that kept running. You have called a large language model API from your own code, not only used a chat app. You use AI coding tools such as Claude Code or Cursor, and you still read every line before you trust it. You like finding the reason a thing broke. What you get Real systems in daily use, with real users who will tell you when something breaks. Direct work with the founder’s office. Hands-on time with a harness that guides AI at every step, which few teams have built. How to apply Send us a GitHub link to something you built. Add three lines on what it does, who used it and the hardest bug you fixed in it. That counts for more than your CV. What do we provide @ Testlify? An inspiring work environment and focused workspace. A performance-driven work culture through collaborative review and feedback. Opportunities and guidance to learn new technologies, share knowledge, and grow within the company and sector. Exposure to complex & challenging projects within an international context. A team of driven and passionate colleagues that strive for top quality. Benefits Health insurance Diversity and inclusion Learn and grow Flexible work hours Saturday & Sunday Week offs Equal opportunities statement Testlify is deeply committed to creating a workplace and global community where inclusion is not only valued but prioritized. We're proud to be an equal-opportunity employer, seeking to create a welcoming and diverse environment. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, gender identity or expression, family status, marital status, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, neurodiversity, disability, age, or any other non-merit-based or legally protected grounds.",
